    "parsing_res_list": [
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "—Thomas B. Macaulay\n\nnever would be found out.",
            "block_bbox": [
                130,
                313,
                450,
                350
            ],
            "block_id": 0,
            "block_order": 1
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "",
            "block_bbox": [
                134,
                366,
                476,
                403
            ],
            "block_id": 1,
            "block_order": 2
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The measure of a man's character is what he would do if he knew the",
            "block_bbox": [
                132,
                397,
                1012,
                454
            ],
            "block_id": 2,
            "block_order": 3
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "—Ralph W. Emerson\n\nThe true test of civilization is, not the census, nor the size of the cities,\n\nnot the corps, but the kind of man that the country turns out.",
            "block_bbox": [
                132,
                491,
                410,
                523
            ],
            "block_id": 3,
            "block_order": 4
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "",
            "block_bbox": [
                133,
                522,
                907,
                568
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 5
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "",
            "block_bbox": [
                133,
                566,
                1039,
                618
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 6
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "—Said Nuri",
            "block_bbox": [
                131,
                653,
                305,
                684
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 7
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Politics with revolves around benefit is savagery.",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                690,
                762,
                726
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 8
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "—Theodore Roosevelt",
            "block_bbox": [
                134,
                764,
                437,
                793
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 9
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "to society.",
            "block_bbox": [
                137,
                809,
                275,
                840
            ],
            "block_id": 9,
            "block_order": 10
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "To educate a man in mind and not in morals is to educate a memace",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                852,
                1002,
                885
            ],
            "block_id": 10,
            "block_order": 11
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "—Martin Lunder King, Jr",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                923,
                460,
                955
            ],
            "block_id": 11,
            "block_order": 12
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "take it because one's conscience tells one that it is right.",
            "block_bbox": [
                137,
                966,
                861,
                999
            ],
            "block_id": 12,
            "block_order": 13
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "take a position that is neither safe, nor politic, nor popular but one must",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                1015,
                1058,
                1049
            ],
            "block_id": 13,
            "block_order": 14
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "asks the question, is it right, And there comes a time when one must",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                1065,
                1040,
                1098
            ],
            "block_id": 14,
            "block_order": 15
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": ", is it politic, Variety asks the question, is it popular, but, conscience",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                1114,
                1037,
                1149
            ],
            "block_id": 15,
            "block_order": 16
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Conwardice asks the question, is it safe? Expediently asks the question,",
            "block_bbox": [
                138,
                1162,
                1050,
                1197
            ],
            "block_id": 16,
            "block_order": 17
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "—Albert Einstein",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                1230,
                366,
                1261
            ],
            "block_id": 17,
            "block_order": 18
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "all technical effort. Never forget it among your diagrams and equations.",
            "block_bbox": [
                136,
                1275,
                1048,
                1314
            ],
            "block_id": 18,
            "block_order": 19
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The concern for man and his destiny must always be the chief interest of",
            "block_bbox": [
                132,
                1327,
                1060,
                1366
            ],
            "block_id": 19,
            "block_order": 20
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "—Manny Hall",
            "block_bbox": [
                134,
                1393,
                314,
                1425
            ],
            "block_id": 20,
            "block_order": 21
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "A man without ethics is a wild beast loosed upon this world.",
            "block_bbox": [
                138,
                1442,
                906,
                1477
            ],
            "block_id": 21,
            "block_order": 22
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "—Laura Schleissinger",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                1508,
                434,
                1545
            ],
            "block_id": 22,
            "block_order": 23
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "doen't mean it's right to do it.",
            "block_bbox": [
                137,
                1558,
                548,
                1593
            ],
            "block_id": 23,
            "block_order": 24
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Because you're able to do it and because you have the right to do it",
            "block_bbox": [
                134,
                1608,
                991,
                1646
            ],
            "block_id": 24,
            "block_order": 25
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "—Jacques Cousteau",
            "block_bbox": [
                133,
                1676,
                425,
                1708
            ],
            "block_id": 25,
            "block_order": 26
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "on a big machinery and nobody is driving the machinery. And it's going faster and faster, but we don't know whether.",
            "block_bbox": [
                135,
                1723,
                690,
                1756
            ],
            "block_id": 26,
            "block_order": 27
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "",
            "block_bbox": [
                132,
                1766,
                1031,
                1815
            ],
            "block_id": 27,
            "block_order": 28
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Without ethics, everything happens as if we were all five billion passengers",
            "block_bbox": [
                133,
                1813,
                1061,
                1868
            ],
            "block_id": 28,
            "block_order": 29
        },
        {
            "block_label": "footer",
            "block_content": "ouches on Ethis",
            "block_bbox": [
                802,
                1890,
                1060,
                1930
            ],
            "block_id": 29,
            "block_order": null
        }
    ],
